\b\f1\insrsid15008363  Identify which of the following are stock variables and which are flow variables?
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid15008363 hese are the terms used to differentiate things like "wealth versus income" or "debt versus deficit."
\par 
\par That is, a "stock variable" is a variable measurable at one particular time (wealth); whereas, a "flow variable" is a variable measured after a prolonged amount of time retrospecting spending in the past "x" amount of time (income).
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx0\tx504\tx720\tx864\tx1224\tx1584\tqr\tx9605\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid15008363 a)\tab Unemployment

