These are the terms used to differentiate things like "wealth versus income" or "debt versus deficit."
\par That is, a "stock variable" is a variable measurable at one particular time (wealth); whereas, a "flow variable" is a variable measured after a prolonged amount of time retrospecting spending in the past "x" amount of time (income).
