\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs22\insrsid15008363 In economics, }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af44\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f44\fs22\insrsid15008363 endogenous growth theory }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs22\insrsid15008363 or }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af44\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f44\fs22\insrsid15008363 new growth theory }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs22\insrsid15008363 was developed in the 1980s as a
\par response to criticism of the neo-classical growth model.
