\b\f1\insrsid15008363  Why countries have comparative advantage according to Ricardo?}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs32\cf1\insrsid15008363 
\par        
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs32\cf1\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15008363 ANSWER:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs32\ul\cf1\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15008363 
\par 
\par Comparative advantage according to Ricardo:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\ul\cf2\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15008363 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15008363 The law of }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15008363 comparative advantage}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15008363  refers to the ability of a party (an individual, a firm, or a country) to produce a particular good or service at a lower }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid15008363 opportunity cost t}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15008363 han another party.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid15008363  There is a  source of comparative advantage can be productivity differentials.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15008363 Ricardo argued that there is mutual benefit from trade (or exchange) even if one party }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15008363 
(e.g. resource rich country, highly-skilled artisan}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15008363 ) is more productive in every possible area than its trading counterpart (e.g. resource-poor country, unskilled labore
r), as long as each concentrates on the activities where it has a relative productivity advantage}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid15008363 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid15008363 
