0000fc020000ffffff000000040000002d01040004000000f0010100040000002701ffff1c000000fb021000070000000000bc02000000000102022253797374656d000000000000fd99807c58bd1e0010f9230070bb1e005ae78339040000002d010100030000000000}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f1\insrsid15008363  What thing determines comparative advantage among countries according to Hechshcer-Ohlin? What is the criticism against their argument?
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid15008363 According to Hechshcer-Ohlin suppose we are given two countries one abundant
\par in labour and one abundant in capital and a labour-intensive good and a capital intensive
\par good, the labour abundant country will have comparative advantage in the production of the labour-intensive good while the capital abundant country will have comparative advantage in the capital-intensive good.
\par So the determinants of comparative advantage among countries according to Hechshcer-Ohlin is capital goods and labour intensive goods.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs28\ul\cf1\insrsid15008363 Critics argued}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid15008363  that comparative advantage can an
d should be viewed in a dynamic (time-varying) sense, and that it was not wise to rule out the possibility of Pakistan developing comparative advantage in cars at some future point in time.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs28\ul\cf1\insrsid15008363 Consequent:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\ul\cf1\insrsid15008363 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\cf1\insrsid15008363 
The major criticism leveled against Hechscher-Ohlin type trade theories are that they views
\par comparative advantage in an essentially static sense; i.e. if Pakistan is better at producing
\par cotton and Japan better at producing, then this situation will always prevail.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\cf1\insrsid15008363 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid15008363 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid15008363 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid15008363 Question No: 49    ( Marks: 3 ) 
