\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\cf1\insrsid15008363 1.      Comments of current account in balance of payment  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\cf1\insrsid15008363         }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\cf1\insrsid15008363 3 marks

\par ANSWER:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af44\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f44\fs22\insrsid15008363 THE CURRENT ACCOUNT
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs22\insrsid15008363 The current account balance is essentially the trade balance (exports minus imports), but with net factor
\par receipts from abroad added.
\par If the exchange rate is fixed, then changes in reserves must mirror the combined balance on the current
\par and capital accounts in order to bring the overall BOPs to zero. If the exchange rate is floating, then
\par changes to reserves can remain zero, as the adjustment burden is borne by the exchange rate which
\par appreciates (depreciates) in response to a joint surplus (deficit) on the current and capital accounts.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\fs22\cf5\insrsid15008363 REFRENCE FOR COMPLETE CONCEPT:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af44\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f44\fs22\insrsid15008363 PARTS OF BOP
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs22\insrsid15008363 The BOPs can be divided into three parts:
\par i. Current account,
\par ii. Capital account and
\par iii. Changes to reserves
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\fs22\cf5\insrsid15008363 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\cf1\insrsid15008363 2.     }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\cf1\insrsid15008363 The reason of poverty in developing countries according Perbisch-Singer Hypothesis
\par ( 3 marks)
\par ANSWER:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid15008363 POVERTY }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f1\fs20\insrsid15008363 means }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid15008363 the state of being poor; lack of the means of providing material needs or comforts.
\par According to }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid15008363 Prebisch-Singer hypothesis following are the reason of poverty in developing countries:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af3 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid15008363 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li720\ri0\sb100\sa100\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn 
\pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnf3 {\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls1\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid15008363 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid15008363 One of the reson for poverty is increasing population.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af3 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid15008363 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0
\pnf3 {\pntxtb \'b7}}\faauto\ls1\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid15008363 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid15008363 Another reason }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af44\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f44\fs22\insrsid15008363 
Lack of precious natural resources (like oil, gold, gas, iron, copper etc.) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af43\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f43\fs22\insrsid15008363 was also cited by some as the reason for LICs\rquote  continued poverty.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid15008363 
